<[Kevin] APPERT> Vesta Forth for the 80196?
<[gars] GARY-S> 83i96
<[80jax196] JAX> We have a new single board computer, the SBC196 ... the 
language for it is Forth-83i96.
<[Kevin] APPERT>  features?
<[80jax196] JAX> All the usual Vesta stuff, pretty much.
<[80jax196] JAX> The uniqueness is twofold:
<[80jax196] JAX> 1) The 80196 is a 16-banger without seg regs ... but 
Forth-83i96 uses a 96-k memory model, and ...
<[80jax196] JAX> 2) The user's code compiled interactively is ROMmable directly,
 without the step of copying back to RAM for execution.
<[80jax196] JAX> The SBC196 is a neat control computer.
<[80jax196] JAX> It has I^2C bus (Philips) and MicroWire bus.
<[80jax196] JAX> Onboard RTC ...
<[80jax196] JAX> Pin connector for offboard access ( 4k of mem map is for 
offboard access)
<[80jax196] JAX> 80C196 has Hi SPeed Inputs and Outputs, PWM generator ...
<[Kevin] APPERT> no experience, myself.  how do you address beyond 64k w/out 
seg regs?
<[80jax196] JAX> LOW POWER BOARD running, about 80 uA ...
<[80jax196] JAX> idle, about 28 uA ...
<[Kevin] APPERT> RTC = time of day or count of clock osc. ticks?
<[80jax196] JAX> 80C196 PowerDown state (re-awaken with extint) is ~ 1uA !!!
<[80jax196] JAX> RTC == Realtime Clock chip, also tick counter in timer int of 
course.
<[80jax196] JAX> Board is ~ 3"x 4".
<[80jax196] JAX> Development configuration is 64K EPROM + 128K SRAM.
<[80jax196] JAX> Runtime configuration for user's ROMmed app is 64K EPROM + 32K 
SRAM.
<[80jax196] JAX> Provides at runtime one of the following two setups:
<[80jax196] JAX> 16K user dictionary + 28K data space + 4K offboard mem-map + 
16K binary code
<[80jax196] JAX> or ...
<[80jax196] JAX> 32K user dictionary + 12K data space + 4K offboard mem-map.
<[Kevin] APPERT> how do you go beyond 64k w/ 16 bits and no seg. regs. ?
<[80jax196] JAX> It's a secret :-)
